o save session state after review env adoption\",\n\t\t\t\t\tslog.String(\"error\", saveErr.Error()))\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n</code></pre></div>\n</details>"},{"url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1105#discussion_r3183190747","body":"Fixed in 252d61d7d. The save guard now uses `slices.Equal(updated.ReviewSkills, state.ReviewSkills)` so any content change (not just length change) triggers a save. (Practical impact today is small because `adoptReviewEnv` short-circuits when `state.Kind != \"\"`, so the only transition is nil→populated; but defensive against future refactors that might remove the idempotency guard.)","user":{"login":"peyton-alt","name":"peyton-alt","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4","id":249787869},"id":3183190747,"pull_request_review_id":4221961622,"in_reply_to_id":3183060208,"created_at":"2026-05-04T17:10:56Z","review":null,"side":"RIGHT","line":287,"start_line":280,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go","body_html":"<p dir=\"auto\">Fixed in <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/commit/252d61d7dea3b94694590f5850b10b9f234cbb51/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/commit/252d61d7dea3b94694590f5850b10b9f234cbb51\"><tt>252d61d</tt></a>. The save guard now uses <code class=\"notranslate\">slices.Equal(updated.ReviewSkills, state.ReviewSkills)</code> so any content change (not just length change) triggers a save. (Practical impact today is small because <code class=\"notranslate\">adoptReviewEnv</code> short-circuits when <code class=\"notranslate\">state.Kind != \"\"</code>, so the only transition is nil→populated; but defensive against future refactors that might remove the idempotency guard.)</p>"},{"url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1105#pullrequestreview-4221961622","body":"","user":{"login":"peyton-alt","name":"peyton-alt","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?u=a3ad5ad82f69e47f529e865376424c6bd35bc305&v=4","id":249787869},"id":4221961622,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-05-04T17:10:57Z","review":"COMMENTED","side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":""},{"url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1105#discussion_r3183192002","body":"Fixed in 252d61d7d via doc updates rather than persistence. Both env vars are still set on the spawned process per the contract. The doc comments on `EnvAgent` and `EnvStartingSHA` in `cmd/entire/cli/review/env.go` now explain the current adoption behavior:\n\n- `EnvAgent` is logged for diagnostics; the agent's identity is already persisted via session state's existing `agent_type` field set during normal turn-start handling.\n- `EnvStartingSHA` is reserved for future consumers (e.g. the re-run guard) and is currently unused by CU1's adoption path because session state's existing `base_commit` field captures the same SHA via normal turn-start handling.\n\nThis eliminates the contract/code mismatch while keeping the env vars on the spawned process for future code that needs them.","user":{"login":"peyton-alt","name":"peyton-alt","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4","id":249787869},"id":3183192002,"pull_request_review_id":4221963100,"in_reply_to_id":3183060272,"created_at":"2026-05-04T17:11:10Z","review":null,"side":"RIGHT","line":1000,"start_line":969,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go","body_html":"<p dir=\"auto\">Fixed in <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/commit/252d61d7dea3b94694590f5850b10b9f234cbb51/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/commit/252d61d7dea3b94694590f5850b10b9f234cbb51\"><tt>252d61d</tt></a> via doc updates rather than persistence. Both env vars are still set on the spawned process per the contract. The doc comments on <code class=\"notranslate\">EnvAgent</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">EnvStartingSHA</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">cmd/entire/cli/review/env.go</code> now explain the current adoption behavior:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">EnvAgent</code> is logged for diagnostics; the agent's identity is already persisted via session state's existing <code class=\"notranslate\">agent_type</code> field set during normal turn-start handling.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">EnvStartingSHA</code> is reserved for future consumers (e.g. the re-run guard) and is currently unused by CU1's adoption path because session state's existing <code class=\"notranslate\">base_commit</code> field captures the same SHA via normal turn-start handling.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This eliminates the contract/code mismatch while keeping the env vars on the spawned process for future code that needs them.</p>"},{"url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1105#pullrequestreview-4221963100","body":"","user":{"login":"peyton-alt","name":"peyton-alt","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?u=a3ad5ad82f69e47f529e865376424c6bd35bc305&v=4","id":249787869},"id":4221963100,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-05-04T17:11:10Z","review":"COMMENTED","side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":""},{"url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1105#discussion_r3183195904","body":"Fixed in 252d61d7d. The test now unmarshals to `map[string]any` and asserts on actual JSON keys (`kind`, `review_skills`, `review_prompt`) — a coordinated rename of struct field + tag would now be caught because the map keys would no longer match the expected literal strings.","user":{"login":"peyton-alt","name":"peyton-alt","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4","id":249787869},"id":3183195904,"pull_request_review_id":4221967732,"in_reply_to_id":3183060312,"created_at":"2026-05-04T17:11:54Z","review":null,"side":"RIGHT","line":4316